    "caption": "Thanks to Gigi Hadid, Vodka Pasta had its moment to shine in social media, and while that trend may have faded, it does not discount the fact that Vodka Pasta is a really delicious pasta dish. And with the help of Murgella Fresh Burrata, the experience is made even more indulgent.\n\nTangy, hearty, and creamy, this Vodka Pasta with Burrata is great for weekend lunches or dinners. Vodka provides a sweet, lingering flavor that contrasts the tangy tomato sauce quite nicely. Find all the ingredients you need for this recipe at #TheMarketplace! \n\nServing Time: 30 minutes\nYield: 2-3 servings\n\nIngredients\n\n400g penne pasta\nSalt and pepper to taste \n2 tbsps. olive oil\n1 tbsp. shallot, minced\n2 tbsps. garlic, minced\n½ tbsp. chili flakes\n¼ cup tomato paste\n1/8 cup vodka\n2 cups heavy cream\n1 cup cherry tomatoes  halved\n¼ cup parmesan cheese, grated\n½ cup basil leaves\n3 pcs. Murgella Fresh Burrata\n\nProcedure\n\n1. Cook penne pasta in heavily salted boiling water until al dente. Save ½ cup of pasta water before draining, then set aside.\n2. Sauté shallots and garlic in olive oil until tender. Add in chili flakes and tomato paste, then cook for 1-2 minutes. \n3. Deglaze pan with vodka. Once most of the vodka has evaporated, mix in heavy cream. Season with salt and pepper to taste.\n4. Mix in cooked penne, along with ½ cup pasta water, cherry tomatoes and parmesan.\n5. Garnish with basil leaves, and top each serving with 1 Murgella Fresh Burrata. Sprinkle salt and pepper over Burrata.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
